From 3b449681ecab190d935b2746686b46edb90e6bab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jgrizon
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:13:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader: VICTORY_WAVE64_REDUCE takes reductions in IR-uniform
 control (off)

The low-rate wave-reduction refusals stop at "a wave reduction over both
32-lane halves" because the reduction's block is not in in_step: the loop
counts are not proven alike, though every branch on the path is on a scalar.

With VICTORY_WAVE64_REDUCE=1, when the reduction is not inside a nested guard
block (cur == level) and every path to its block goes through scalar branches
only (barriers::uniform_control), the halves reduce their own 32 lanes and
exchange the result through threadgroup memory with a group barrier (the
existing reduce_across) instead of refusing or answering from one half. Lane
branches still refuse: they split the wave, and a barrier there could hang.
Off by default; part of the shader cache key.

Ported from paveledits/ScarlettMac runtime-preview/checkpoint/patches/0013-shader-VICTORY_WAVE64_REDUCE-takes-reductions-in-IR-.patch

